      "final_response": "## Diagnosis\n\nThe bug was in `claims.go` in the `ValidateClaims` function:\n\n```go\nreturn !c.Valid  // inverted — returns true when claims are invalid\n```\n\nThis meant valid claims (`Valid: true`) → `ValidateClaims` returned `false` → `Authenticate` returned `ErrUnauthorized`. Only invalid claims (`Valid: false`) were being \"authenticated\" successfully — the exact opposite of intended behavior.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `return !c.Valid` to `return c.Valid`, restoring the correct semantics.\n\n## Test Result\n\n```\n=== RUN   TestAuthenticate\n--- PASS: TestAuthenticate (0.00s)\nPASS\nok  \tacme/auth\t0.342s\n```\n\nBoth test cases now pass: valid claims authenticate cleanly, and invalid claims correctly return `ErrUnauthorized`.",
